<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sudeten German Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933–1938</span> · Also known as Sudetendeutsche Partei</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sudeten German Party was the political party of the German minority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-henlein">Konrad Henlein</a> in 1933 as the Sudeten German Home Front and renamed in 1935. Winning more votes than any other party in the 1935 elections, it was increasingly directed and funded by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its demands for autonomy led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich-agreement">Munich Agreement</a>, and it merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a> in late 1938.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sudeten-german-party.jpg" alt="Sudeten German Party" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FDRMRZUSA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Sudeten_German_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
